{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type SuspenseQueriesOptions<T, TResults, TDepth> = TDepth[\"length\"] extends MAXIMUM_DEPTH ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions[] : T extends [] ? [] : T extends [infer Head] ? [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>] : T extends [infer Head, ...(infer Tails)] ? SuspenseQueriesOptions<[...Tails], [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>], [...TDepth, 1]> : unknown[] extends T ? T : T extends UseSuspenseQueryOptions<infer TQueryFnData, infer TError, infer TData, infer TQueryKey>[] ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>[] : UseSuspenseQueryOptions[];","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts#L122","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts:122"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queries"},{"type":"text","value":" array accepted by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSuspenseQueries"},{"type":"text","value":". Recursively unwraps each tuple element so every\nentry's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"select"},{"type":"text","value":" are inferred individually, up to 20 elements — past that, a tuple falls back to\na single homogeneous "},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/UseSuspenseQueryOptions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"UseSuspenseQueryOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An opaque array (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown[]"},{"type":"text","value":") is returned as-is; a non-tuple array whose element type structurally\nmatches a query options object is mapped per-element instead, still inferring each entry individually; any\nother non-tuple array — one whose element type doesn't match the expected options shape — falls back to\nthat same homogeneous options type too."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"t","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"T"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":"[]"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queries"},{"type":"text","value":" array as written at the call site."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tresults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TResults"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TResults"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":"[] = []"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The internal accumulator that this type builds during recursion. It is not meant\nto be set explicitly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tdepth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TDepth"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TDepth"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ReadonlyArray"},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"},{"type":"text","value":"> = []"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The internal recursion-depth counter, checked against the 20-element limit. It is not\nmeant to be set explicitly."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"t","text":"T","level":3},{"id":"tresults","text":"TResults","level":3},{"id":"tdepth","text":"TDepth","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype SuspenseQueriesOptions<T, TResults, TDepth> = TDepth[\"length\"] extends MAXIMUM_DEPTH ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions[] : T extends [] ? [] : T extends [infer Head] ? [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>] : T extends [infer Head, ...(infer Tails)] ? SuspenseQueriesOptions<[...Tails], [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>], [...TDepth, 1]> : unknown[] extends T ? T : T extends UseSuspenseQueryOptions<infer TQueryFnData, infer TError, infer TData, infer TQueryKey>[] ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>[] : UseSuspenseQueryOptions[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts:122](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts#L122)\n\nThe `queries` array accepted by `useSuspenseQueries`. Recursively unwraps each tuple element so every\nentry's `queryFn`/`select` are inferred individually, up to 20 elements — past that, a tuple falls back to\na single homogeneous [UseSuspenseQueryOptions](../interfaces/UseSuspenseQueryOptions.md) type.\n\nAn opaque array (e.g. `unknown[]`) is returned as-is; a non-tuple array whose element type structurally\nmatches a query options object is mapped per-element instead, still inferring each entry individually; any\nother non-tuple array — one whose element type doesn't match the expected options shape — falls back to\nthat same homogeneous options type too.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `any`[]\n\nThe type of the `queries` array as written at the call site.\n\n### TResults\n\n`TResults` *extends* `any`[] = \\[\\]\n\nThe internal accumulator that this type builds during recursion. It is not meant\nto be set explicitly.\n\n### TDepth\n\n`TDepth` *extends* `ReadonlyArray`\\<`number`\\> = \\[\\]\n\nThe internal recursion-depth counter, checked against the 20-element limit. It is not\nmeant to be set explicitly.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: SuspenseQueriesOptions\ntitle: SuspenseQueriesOptions\n---\n\n```ts\ntype SuspenseQueriesOptions<T, TResults, TDepth> = TDepth[\"length\"] extends MAXIMUM_DEPTH ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions[] : T extends [] ? [] : T extends [infer Head] ? [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>] : T extends [infer Head, ...(infer Tails)] ? SuspenseQueriesOptions<[...Tails], [...TResults, GetUseSuspenseQueryOptions<Head>], [...TDepth, 1]> : unknown[] extends T ? T : T extends UseSuspenseQueryOptions<infer TQueryFnData, infer TError, infer TData, infer TQueryKey>[] ? UseSuspenseQueryOptions<TQueryFnData, TError, TData, TQueryKey>[] : UseSuspenseQueryOptions[];\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts:122](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/preact-query/src/useSuspenseQueries.ts#L122)\n\nThe `queries` array accepted by `useSuspenseQueries`. Recursively unwraps each tuple element so every\nentry's `queryFn`/`select` are inferred individually, up to 20 elements — past that, a tuple falls back to\na single homogeneous [UseSuspenseQueryOptions](../interfaces/UseSuspenseQueryOptions.md) type.\n\nAn opaque array (e.g. `unknown[]`) is returned as-is; a non-tuple array whose element type structurally\nmatches a query options object is mapped per-element instead, still inferring each entry individually; any\nother non-tuple array — one whose element type doesn't match the expected options shape — falls back to\nthat same homogeneous options type too.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### T\n\n`T` *extends* `any`[]\n\nThe type of the `queries` array as written at the call site.\n\n### TResults\n\n`TResults` *extends* `any`[] = \\[\\]\n\nThe internal accumulator that this type builds during recursion. It is not meant\nto be set explicitly.\n\n### TDepth\n\n`TDepth` *extends* `ReadonlyArray`\\<`number`\\> = \\[\\]\n\nThe internal recursion-depth counter, checked against the 20-element limit. It is not\nmeant to be set explicitly.\n"}
